  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Tied through six innings until the seventh inning flipped the game.",
    "what_this_means": "Two runners on, one out, still knotted at one. McMahon's single turned deficit into lead. That swing changed what was possible. A tight game became a game the Yankees could finish. Weathers had given them the platform: five and two-thirds innings, one run, four strikeouts. That was enough to stay in it. The bullpen held what mattered. Hill and Headrick and Bednar combined for three and a third clean innings. Tim Hill pitched 1.1 scoreless. Bednar locked down the save. The lineup came through when it counted. Grisham had two hits and two RBI. Garc\u00eda had two hits. The eight hits and eight strikeouts told the story of a team that didn't dominate but didn't fold. They were down and then they weren't. Late rallies are becoming what they do.",
    "what_to_watch": "SEA's average sits at .228. Warren takes the ball tonight against Bryce Miller, who's carried a 3.08 ERA into the matchup.",
